{"number":1,"title":"Number Systems","slug":"number-systems","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 9 IMO — Number Systems: rational vs irrational numbers, decimal expansions, locating surds on the number line, laws of exponents and rationalising denominators.","topics":[{"title":"Rational and Irrational Numbers","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is a Number Line?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">A number line is a straight line with numbers placed at equal intervals. It helps us visualize the order and relationships between different types of numbers.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Types of Numbers on the Number Line:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Number Type</th><th>Definition</th><th>Examples</th><th>Position on Number Line</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Whole Numbers**</td><td>Natural numbers including 0</td><td>0, 1, 2, 3, ...</td><td>Zero at center, all others right</td></tr><tr><td>**Integers**</td><td>Whole numbers and their negatives</td><td>..., -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, ...</td><td>Both left (negative) and right (positive) of zero</td></tr><tr><td>**Rational Numbers**</td><td>Numbers that can be expressed as p/q where q ≠ 0</td><td>1/2, -3/4, 2.5, 0.333...</td><td>Between integers also, infinitely dense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Important Properties:</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Every point on the number line represents a <strong>real number</strong></li><li>Between any two distinct rational numbers, there are infinitely more rational numbers</li><li>The number line extends infinitely in both directions</li></ul><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#eff6ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dbeafe\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Number Line — Types of Numbers</text><defs><marker id=\"arr\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z\" fill=\"#1e293b\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arr)\"/><text x=\"610\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">→</text><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">-3</text><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">-2</text><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">-1</text><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">0</text><line x1=\"420\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"420\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1</text><line x1=\"500\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2</text><line x1=\"580\" y1=\"173\" x2=\"580\" y2=\"187\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"580\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"210\" width=\"480\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" opacity=\"0.6\" fill=\"#bfdbfe\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e40af\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Integers (Z): ..., -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, ...</text><rect x=\"340\" y=\"245\" width=\"240\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" opacity=\"0.6\" fill=\"#bbf7d0\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Whole Numbers (W): 0,1,2,...</text><rect x=\"360\" y=\"280\" width=\"200\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" opacity=\"0.6\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Natural (N): 1,2,3,...</text><circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"380\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3/4</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Real Numbers (R) = Rationals ∪ Irrationals</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#64748b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Every point on the number line is a Real Number</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Is 0.75 rational?","solution":"Yes — 0.75 = 3/4, a ratio of two integers."},{"number":"2","problem":"Why is √2 irrational?","solution":"Its decimal 1.41421356… never terminates or repeats, so it equals no p/q."}],"recap":["Rational = p/q with integers p, q and q ≠ 0.","Irrational decimals are non-terminating and non-recurring (√2, π)."],"quiz":[{"q":"The decimal representation of the rational number 8/25 is:","options":["0.32","0.25","0.36","0.032"],"correct":0,"explanation":"8/25 = 32/100 = 0.32, a terminating decimal.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"When 0.4777… (7 repeating) is written in p/q form (q ≠ 0), its value is:","options":["47/90","43/90","47/99","43/99"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Let x = 0.4777…; then 10x = 4.777… and 100x = 47.777…. Subtracting, 90x = 43, so x = 43/90.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Decimal Expansions and the Number Line","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What are Terminating and Recurring Decimals?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">When we convert a rational number (p/q) to decimal form by dividing p by q, we get either:</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Terminating Decimals:</strong> The division ends after a finite number of steps.</p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Example: 1/2 = 0.5, 3/4 = 0.75, 7/8 = 0.875</li><li>Occurs when denominator (in simplest form) has only prime factors 2 and 5</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Recurring (Repeating) Decimals:</strong> The division never ends; a digit or block of digits repeats forever.</p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Example: 1/3 = 0.333..., 2/7 = 0.285714285714...</li><li>Represented with a bar: 0.3̅, 0.285714̅</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Why Do Recurring Decimals Occur?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">When denominator has prime factors other than 2 and 5 (like 3, 7, 11, etc.), the decimal repeats.</p><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 345\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f0fdf4\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dcfce7\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rational Numbers &amp; Decimal Expansions</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"60\" width=\"280\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#86efac\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Terminating Decimals</text><rect x=\"330\" y=\"60\" width=\"280\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#fca5a5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"470\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Non-Terminating Repeating</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1/2</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.5</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3/4</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.75</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">7/8</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.875</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1/5</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.2</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1/3</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.333...</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2/7</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.285714...</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">5/6</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.8333...</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1/11</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= 0.0909...</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"275\" width=\"580\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fefce8\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rule: p/q terminates ⟺ q has only 2s and 5s as prime factors</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#64748b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Otherwise it repeats. Both types are RATIONAL.</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Classify 0.142857142857…","solution":"It recurs, so it is rational (it equals 1/7)."},{"number":"2","problem":"How is √2 marked on the number line?","solution":"Draw a unit right triangle; its hypotenuse measures √2, then arc that length onto the line."}],"recap":["Terminating or recurring ⇒ rational; non-recurring ⇒ irrational.","√2, √3, √5 are placed using right-triangle (Pythagoras) constructions."],"quiz":[{"q":"If √2 = 1.4142, then 1/√2 is closest to:","options":["0.7071","1.4142","0.5000","0.4142"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1/√2 = √2/2 = 1.4142/2 = 0.7071.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"The rationalising factor of ∛5 is:","options":["∛5","∛25","√5","5"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Multiplying ∛5 by ∛25 = ∛(5²) gives ∛(5³) = 5, which is rational.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Exponents and Rationalising Denominators","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is Rationalization?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">Rationalization is the process of eliminating irrational numbers (like √2, √3) from the denominator of a fraction. This makes expressions easier to work with and compare.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Why Rationalize?</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>To simplify expressions</li><li>To add/subtract fractions with irrational denominators</li><li>To compare numbers easily</li><li>Standard form in mathematics often requires rationalized denominators</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Methods for Rationalization:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type of Denominator</th><th>Multiply Numerator & Denominator by</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>a + √b</td><td>a - √b (conjugate)</td><td>Denominator becomes a² - b</td></tr><tr><td>√a + √b</td><td>√a - √b (conjugate)</td><td>Denominator becomes a - b</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>The Conjugate Trick:</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">The conjugate of (a + √b) is (a - √b). Their product:</p><p class=\"eb-p\">(a + √b)(a - √b) = a² - (√b)² = a² - b (a rational number)</p><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 415\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f0f9ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#e0f2fe\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#0284c7\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Rationalisation of the Denominator</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"70\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#1d4ed8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Start</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1 / (√3 + √2)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">↓</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"126\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Multiply by conjugate</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">× (√3 - √2) / (√3 - √2)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">↓</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"182\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#d97706\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Numerator</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= (√3 - √2)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">↓</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"238\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fce7f3\" stroke=\"#be185d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#be185d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Denominator</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= (√3)² - (√2)² = 3 - 2 = 1</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">↓</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"294\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ede9fe\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Result</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">= √3 - √2  (Rationalised!)</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"358\" width=\"580\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"383\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Formula: 1/(a+√b) = (a-√b)/((a²-b))</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Rationalise 1/√5.","solution":"Multiply by √5/√5 to get √5/5."},{"number":"2","problem":"Find a rational number between √2 and √3.","solution":"Since √2 ≈ 1.41 and √3 ≈ 1.73, the number 1.5 = 3/2 lies between them."}],"recap":["Surds follow aᵐ · aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ and a^(1/n) = ⁿ√a.","Rationalise by multiplying by the conjugate of the denominator."],"quiz":[{"q":"A Metro train travels at a speed of 3 × ∛216 km/hr. Its actual speed is:","options":["18 km/hr","24 km/hr","36 km/hr","12 km/hr"],"correct":0,"explanation":"∛216 = 6, so speed = 3 × 6 = 18 km/hr.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"A farm has area 7^x square units and an adjacent plot 7^(x−2) square units. If their areas differ by 2352 square units, find x.","options":["3","4","5","2"],"correct":1,"explanation":"7^(x−2)(7² − 1) = 2352, so 7^(x−2) × 48 = 2352 and 7^(x−2) = 49 = 7². Thus x − 2 = 2 and x = 4.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"hard"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":20,"questions":[{"q":"If a > b and b > c, then a > c. This property is called:","options":["Closure property","Commutative property","Associative property","Transitive property"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A relation that carries from a–b and b–c to a–c is the transitive property.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Container A has (√50 + √18) litres of milk and Container B has √32 litres. Poured together, the total milk is:","options":["12√2 liters","8√2 liters","16√2 liters","10√2 liters"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A = 5√2 + 3√2 = 8√2 and B = 4√2, so total = 12√2 litres.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Rationalise the denominator of 6 / (3√2 − 2√3):","options":["3√2 + 2√3","√2 + √3","3√2 − 2√3","2√2 + 3√3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Multiply by (3√2 + 2√3): 6(3√2 + 2√3) / ((3√2)² − (2√3)²) = 6(3√2 + 2√3)/(18 − 12) = 3√2 + 2√3.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"Point P is at √2, Q at √8 and R at √18 from zero. If the pattern continues, the next point S is at:","options":["√24 units","√32 units","√28 units","4 units"],"correct":1,"explanation":"√2, √8 = 2√2, √18 = 3√2, so the next is 4√2 = √32.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"The value of (64/125)^(−2/3) is:","options":["16/25","25/16","4/5","5/4"],"correct":1,"explanation":"(64/125)^(−2/3) = (125/64)^(2/3) = ((5/4)³)^(2/3) = (5/4)² = 25/16.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If 4^x − 4^(x−1) = 24, then the value of (2x)² is:","options":["5","25","125","10"],"correct":1,"explanation":"4^(x−1)(4 − 1) = 24, so 4^(x−1) = 8 = 2³, giving 2x − 2 = 3 and x = 5/2. Then (2x)² = 5² = 25.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"Find the missing term in the sequence: 2, √5, √6, √7, 2√2, …","options":["3","√11","√10","2√3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Writing each term under a root: √4, √5, √6, √7, √8. The next term is √9 = 3.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Which of the following is an irrational number?","options":["√(4/9)","√12 / √3","√7","4.333… (3 repeating)"],"correct":2,"explanation":"√(4/9) = 2/3, √12/√3 = √4 = 2, and 4.333… = 13/3 are rational. √7 cannot be simplified to a rational, so it is irrational.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Simplify: [ { (625)^(−1/2) }^(−1/4) ]²","options":["5","25","1/5","1"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Multiply the powers: (−1/2) × (−1/4) × 2 = 1/4. Then (625)^(1/4) = (5⁴)^(1/4) = 5.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"If x = 9 − 4√5, then √x is:","options":["√5 − 2","2 − √5","√5 + 2","5 − √2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"9 − 4√5 = (√5)² + 2² − 2(2)(√5) = (√5 − 2)², so √x = √5 − 2.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"If 2^x = 3^y = 6^(−z), then 1/x + 1/y + 1/z equals:","options":["0","1","6","−1"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Let 2^x = 3^y = 6^(−z) = k. Then 2 = k^(1/x), 3 = k^(1/y), 6 = k^(−1/z). Since 2 × 3 = 6, k^(1/x + 1/y) = k^(−1/z), so 1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"What is the value of (2⁰ + 7¹ + 5³) / (11⁰ × 2³)?","options":["133/8","132/8","125/8","17"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Numerator = 1 + 7 + 125 = 133; denominator = 1 × 8 = 8; value = 133/8.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A circular garden has radius √7 m. If the radius is increased to 3√7 m, how many times does the area increase?","options":["3 times","6 times","9 times","27 times"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Area is proportional to radius². The radius becomes 3 times, so the area becomes 3² = 9 times.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A rectangular rug has length 4√3 m and width 2√3 m. Its area is:","options":["24 square meters","8 square meters","12 square meters","16 square meters"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Area = 4√3 × 2√3 = 8 × 3 = 24 square metres.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"In the sequence P₁ = √3, P₂ = √12, P₃ = √27, P₄ = √48, the next term P₅ is:","options":["√63","√75","√108","√60"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The terms are 1√3, 2√3, 3√3, 4√3, so the next is 5√3 = √(25 × 3) = √75.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]}}}